# Precision-convergence audit for the decimal Nyström reference

Independently reconstruct the strictly positive near-coincident 4-by-4 RBF center matrices at 80, 100, and 120 decimal digits for separations `1e-6`, `1e-7`, and `1e-8`. Record the maximum decimal residual of the 120-digit inverse and the relative change of the projected kernel between successive precisions after conversion to float64. The high-precision boundary evidence is accepted only if every inverse residual is below `1e-60` and every 100-to-120-digit projected-kernel change is below `1e-12` relative Frobenius norm. Serial CPU-only execution uses the unchanged 4-GiB guard.
